# UI Consistency, Language & Component Reuse

## 1. Language

- **UI text must be in English** — all labels, placeholders, buttons, messages, errors, toasts, and any user-facing strings.
- AI agent responses may be in Vietnamese.

## 2. Toast Feedback (Sonner)

- Use `toast` from `sonner` for **all** user feedback — success, error, warning, loading, info.
- Never use raw HTML/CSS alert boxes or inline messages for user feedback.
- Import: `import { toast } from 'sonner';`
- Examples:

```tsx
// Success
toast.success('Password reset successfully!');

// Error
toast.error('Failed to send reset email. Please try again.');

// Loading
toast.loading('Sending email...');

// Info
toast.info('Check your inbox for the reset link.');
```

## 3. Reuse Existing Components

- Check `src/components/ui/` and `src/components/features/` before writing any new UI code.
- Use shadcn/ui components:
  - `Button` from `@/components/ui/button`
  - `Dialog`, `AlertDialog` from `@/components/ui/dialog`
  - `Input`, `Label` from `@/components/ui/input`
  - `DropdownMenu` from `@/components/ui/dropdown-menu`
  - `Select` from `@/components/ui/select`
  - Skeleton components from `src/components/ui/skeletons/`
- For icons: use `lucide-react` (already installed)

## 4. Never Create New Components Unnecessarily

- Do not create custom modals, dialogs, alerts, buttons, or toasts from scratch.
- Wrap existing shadcn/ui primitives instead.
- Only create a new component file when no existing component can be adapted.

## Anti-patterns

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Custom alert overlay
<div className="fixed inset-0 bg-black/40">
  <div className="bg-white p-4">Confirm?</div>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — Reuse AlertDialog
import { AlertDialog, AlertDialogAction, AlertDialogCancel, AlertDialogContent, AlertDialogDescription, AlertDialogFooter, AlertDialogHeader, AlertDialogTitle } from '@/components/ui/alert-dialog';
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Inline error message
<p className="text-red-500">Something went wrong.</p>

// ✅ GOOD — Toast
import { toast } from 'sonner';
toast.error('Something went wrong.');
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Custom button
<button className="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-lg">Submit</button>

// ✅ GOOD — Reuse Button
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
<Button>Submit</Button>
```
